   "properties": {
    "Node name for S&R": "Note"
   },
   "widgets_values": [
    "⚗ CALIBRATE YOUR MODEL\n\n1. Pick YOUR Krea 2 checkpoint in the first node.\n2. Set the FINAL resolution you will use here (3 MP = ~1408x2112).\n3. Queue once: the 4 nodes measure 4 different prompts (portrait,\n   half body, full figure, still life) and average them into the same\n   profile 'krea2_nvfp4_3MP' (mode 'accumula' = accumulate).\n4. Press R in the browser: the profile appears in the sampler's\n   'profilo' menu. The last report holds the averaged values.\n\nTo start from scratch: set 'sostituisci' (replace) in the first node.\nMore prompts of your own = better profile (change the texts, re-run).\n\nOPTIONAL: connect 'modello_riferimento' to a second UNETLoader with\nkrea2_turbo_fp8_scaled: it measures how far NVFP4 drifts from FP8\nat each sigma (slow: ComfyUI swaps the two models in VRAM).\n\nRead the GPU/torch/CUDA line of the report: on Blackwell GPUs NVFP4\nruns at full speed only with PyTorch built for CUDA 13.0 (cu130)."
   ],
   "title": "⚗ AlchemicaMente · notes"
  }
